qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (complete; investigation only)\n\nOBSERVATION\nThe ticket reports that `attach_commits` successfully recorded merged SHA `ea394c34...` on `goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle`, but the close precheck still failed with “no commit references it.” Code inspection matches: attached commits are read by `_attached_commit_shas`, but not considered by the presence check that decides whether work “landed.”\n\nHYPOTHESIS\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_work_landed` computes `referencing = _referencing_commits(...)` and raises when `own_impact and not referencing`. The function calls `_check_file_impact_vs_diff(...)` only after that raise point. The attached-commit source is unioned later inside `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_file_impact_vs_diff`, so attachments can validate diff impact but cannot satisfy the earlier “at least one landed commit exists” predicate.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nConfirmed with a deterministic monkeypatch experiment: `_union_file_impact` and `field_reads.file_impact` returned `['src/a.py']`, `_referencing_commits` returned `[]`, `_attached_commit_shas` returned `['attached-sha']`, and `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` was instrumented. `_check_work_landed(...)` raised the existing “no commit references it” error and the diff checker was never called (`DIFF_CALLS 0`). This would have been disproven if the attached SHA had been unioned into the presence decision or if the diff checker had run.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nMake `_check_work_landed` decide presence over the union of trailer-discovered commits and valid attached commits, while keeping the existing asymmetric unreadable-SHA policy and the later file-impact validation over both sources.","timestamp":1788737387721494001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review initially BLOCKED on missing verification-presence. Added a Testing / Verification section naming the RED regression selector, GREEN focused tests, and final make verify plan; re-running plan review once as instructed.","timestamp":1788745241816135001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED confirmed: tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_work_landed_credits_valid_attached_commit_for_presence failed because _check_work_landed raised the existing no-referencing-commit error before attached commits reached diff validation. GREEN confirmed: new selector plus unreadable-attached and close-precheck message coverage passed; full tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py passed (27 tests).","timestamp":1788745749617062001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed fix in worktree fix2-smoggy: 59888f18709d. verify-commit-ticket passed. Starting make verify before Gerrit push.","timestamp":1788745850511500001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify completed successfully in fix2-smoggy and change pushed to Gerrit as 2731.","timestamp":1788749039180099001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2731 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with no unresolved comments, then was submitted/merged. AC boxes marked complete; closing against merged ref 9444cd783ea36cd939e5561f7c64ec09e90099d2 as regression.","timestamp":1788751071909872001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788735407771398437,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"32330452-03ad-4e1b-b9a9-68b86749900c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"36f4-ae53-2199-42c1"},{"link_uuid":"ad747d5f-b7d9-444c-8d88-d667f0c215a2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0541-5c0b-2bfe-4d2b"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`attach_commits` is documented as the repair path that lets the close gate tie a ticket to a landed change when no usable trailer can be discovered. During closure of `goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle`, attaching the valid merged SHA `ea394c34d13745cc0a14cea968b32f435ef15711` succeeded and the ticket state showed it under `commits`, but the deterministic close precheck still failed with “no commit references it.”\n\nThe implementation explains the contradiction: `_check_work_landed` rejects when `_referencing_commits(...)` is empty before `_attached_commit_shas(...)` is considered. Attached SHAs are used only by the later file-impact-vs-diff check.\n\n## Approach\nMake the work-landed presence decision use the union of trailer-discovered commits and validated ticket-attached commits, while retaining the existing path-impact validation and unreadable-commit policy. Add regression coverage through the close-precheck seam.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A file-impact ticket with a valid attached implementation commit passes the deterministic “work landed” presence check when no trailer-discovered commit is reachable from HEAD.\n- [x] Attached and trailer-discovered commits are both checked against the declared file impact.\n- [x] An absent attachment and absent trailer-discovered commit still fails closed with the existing actionable error.\n- [x] An unreadable attached SHA retains the documented cross-clone behavior.\n- [x] Tests cover the repaired close-precheck behavior without weakening normal trailer scanning.\n\n## Evidence\nObserved on ticket `36f4-ae53-2199-42c1`. Relevant seams: `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py::_check_work_landed`, `_attached_commit_shas`, and `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- RED: add a unit regression in `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py` (or the close-precheck unit module if that is where the seam already lives) proving `_check_work_landed` currently fails when `_referencing_commits` is empty but `_attached_commit_shas` returns a valid attached implementation commit for a file-impact ticket.\n- GREEN: run the new focused pytest selector and the existing attach/close-precheck tests that cover trailer-discovered commits, missing commits, file-impact checks, and unreadable attached SHAs.\n- Final verification: run `make verify` before Gerrit push.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0541-5c0b-2bfe-4d2b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6154d587-3726-46f4-833d-f213583ec706","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bug","completion-gate","commit-traceability"],"ticket_id":"5623-98ad-dc87-49fa","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Close gate ignores attached commits for landing proof","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9ec4a653-7a92-4bfd-9843-595322118ec7","9f8ce9e4-a2a1-40d0-98d4-63b51ee944f2","426da903-2545-45b1-99c5-0afae70bfa3e","971bc396-51e5-4f92-9ac9-ad7934c22698","46862a0f-1d41-41e1-aceb-06e6ca6a222b","52b7eff5-319b-45a1-8a50-6a7dd627f52a","6fa85117-6389-4d4a-83af-05fd59d7be9a","40c0f191-ea03-476e-a88a-a55bad419cc1","ad747d5f-b7d9-444c-8d88-d667f0c215a2","b8b9390b-82b5-4e50-8e85-7d19562557ee","b38ea7f9-6336-4f59-805d-36e3453e96d9","6154d587-3726-46f4-833d-f213583ec706","b56635eb-f64f-4fbf-8c1b-cc4c66ce8fd7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788761040058314001,"uuid":"4182f1fa-4c43-409d-8b59-36bab461ebe9"}